horrific footage verified by chinese  state media shows the aircraft nose  diving to the ground in the remote  southern province of guangxi  the passenger plane operated by china  eastern airlines departed from the city  of kunming just after 1pm local time  it was headed to the city of guangzhou a  route which should have taken less than  two hours  when it suddenly lost altitude dropping  more than 6 000 meters in just two  minutes  videos circulating on social media show  a wildfire reportedly sparked by the  crash  the 132 people on board including 123  passengers and nine crew members are  feared dead  hundreds of emergency workers have been  dispatched to the site president xi  jinping has called for an immediate  investigation  analysts say the boeing model 737-800  aircraft has a good safety record the  737 800 has been uh workhorse and i  believe that  china eastern have  over 600 jet aircraft and  i think they've got um somewhere along  the lines of  137.37 so  it's a very reliable aircraft and  it's uh it's quite a amazing story that  an aircraft can crash on a two-hour  flight  the boeing 737 800 is a predecessor of  the 737 max a model that has been banned  from commercial use in china after two  crashes within months that killed 346  people in indonesia and ethiopia  the crash is china's worst aviation  disaster in years its safety record has  been among the best in the world for a  decade  though experts have questioned the  reporting of safety lapses china eastern  airlines says it's mourning the loss of  those on board and has grounded all of  its boeing 737-800 aircraft until  further notice  katrina you al jazeera beijing
 

